{"title":"Career Roadmap · Advocacy Officer","role":"Advocacy Officer","summary":"An Advocacy Officer works to influence policies, institutions, public opinion, and decision-makers on social, human-rights, humanitarian, environmental, development, or public-interest issues.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts – General / Honours)","Course":"Peace & Conflict Studies / Human Rights"},"about":[{"label":"Career Type","text":"NGO / Human Rights / Public Policy / Development / International Organisations"},{"label":"Degree Alignment","text":"Excellent"},{"label":"Typical Entry Level","text":"Advocacy Assistant, Programme Assistant, Policy/Research Assistant, Campaign Coordinator"},{"label":"Long-Term Roles","text":"Advocacy Officer → Senior Advocacy Officer → Advocacy Manager → Policy & Advocacy Lead → Director/Head of Advocacy"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Advocacy Officer works to influence policies, institutions, public opinion, and decision-makers on social, human-rights, humanitarian, environmental, development, or public-interest issues."},{"type":"p","text":"For a student specialising in Peace & Conflict Studies / Human Rights, this is a highly relevant career because the degree develops understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human rights and international norms"},{"text":"Conflict and peacebuilding"},{"text":"Governance and institutions"},{"text":"Social justice"},{"text":"International relations"},{"text":"Public policy"},{"text":"Civil society"},{"text":"Humanitarian issues"},{"text":"Marginalised communities"},{"text":"Research and evidence-based policy"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["The strongest candidates combine subject knowledge","research","policy analysis","communication","campaign/project management","data skills."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"“Advocacy Officer” is generally a private-sector/NGO/development-sector job title rather than a regulated profession. A BA can provide direct entry, although specialised policy, human-rights and international-organisation positions often prefer postgraduate qualifications and relevant field experience."}]},{"heading":"What Does an Advocacy Officer Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Advocacy Officer converts evidence and organisational objectives into actions designed to influence decision-makers and public discourse."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical responsibilities"},{"type":"table","header":["Area","Work"],"rows":[[{"text":"Policy research"},{"text":"Study laws, policies, regulations and government programmes"}],[{"text":"Human rights"},{"text":"Monitor rights-related developments and document concerns"}],[{"text":"Stakeholder engagement"},{"text":"Work with NGOs, government, media, researchers and communities"}],[{"text":"Campaigns"},{"text":"Design and coordinate advocacy campaigns"}],[{"text":"Policy briefs"},{"text":"Prepare evidence-based recommendations"}],[{"text":"Government engagement"},{"text":"Communicate with policymakers and officials"}],[{"text":"Public communication"},{"text":"Prepare statements, reports, articles and presentations"}],[{"text":"Coalitions"},{"text":"Coordinate networks of organisations"}],[{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Collect and analyse qualitative and quantitative evidence"}],[{"text":"Events"},{"text":"Organise consultations, roundtables and policy discussions"}],[{"text":"Monitoring"},{"text":"Track policy changes and advocacy outcomes"}],[{"text":"Reporting"},{"text":"Prepare donor, programme and impact reports"}]]}]},{"heading":"Career Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Typical Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"During UG"},{"text":"Advocacy Intern, Research Intern, Human Rights Intern, Programme Intern"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Advocacy Assistant, Programme Assistant, Research Assistant, Campaign Coordinator"}],[{"text":"1–4 years"},{"text":