d content. Human judgement, community trust, ethics, context, negotiation and evidence verification remain critical."}]},{"heading":"Emerging Careers","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This degree can eventually lead to newer roles such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI Policy Analyst"},{"text":"Digital Rights Advocate"},{"text":"AI Governance Associate"},{"text":"Human Rights Data Analyst"},{"text":"Policy Data Analyst"},{"text":"Climate Justice Advocate"},{"text":"ESG & Human Rights Analyst"},{"text":"Responsible AI Policy Associate"},{"text":"Geopolitical Risk Analyst"},{"text":"Humanitarian Data Analyst"},{"text":"Social Impact Analyst"},{"text":"Public Affairs Specialist"},{"text":"Government Relations Analyst"},{"text":"Conflict Data Analyst"},{"text":"Peacebuilding Programme Specialist"}]}]},{"heading":"Ideal Graduate Profile","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, an excellent candidate should be able to say:"},{"type":"p","text":"“I understand human-rights and conflict issues, can conduct research, analyse evidence, write policy briefs, design advocacy campaigns, work with stakeholders, manage programmes and use data/AI tools to support evidence-based advocacy.”"},{"type":"h","text":"Target profile"},{"type":"table","header":["Area","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"BA Peace & Conflict/Human Rights"}],[{"text":"Internships"},{"text":"2–3"}],[{"text":"Research projects"},{"text":"3+"}],[{"text":"Policy briefs"},{"text":"3–5"}],[{"text":"Advocacy campaigns"},{"text":"1–2"}],[{"text":"Data dashboards"},{"text":"1–2"}],[{"text":"Research tools"},{"text":"Excel + Power BI + survey tools"}],[{"text":"Writing"},{"text":"Policy briefs + reports"}],[{"text":"Field experience"},{"text":"At least 1 meaningful project"}],[{"text":"PG"},{"text":"Strongly useful for specialised roles"}],[{"text":"AI"},{"text":"Research + analytics + policy applications"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Best Practical Path"},{"type":"h","text":"B